From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iAmMichaelConnor <mike@aztec.foundation>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:42:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat!: discover note nonces across the four nonce index
 sections

A note hash's nonce index lies in a fixed, MAX_NOTE_HASHES_PER_TX-wide section
chosen by where the note hash came from: private non-revertible (i), public
non-revertible (MAX + p), private revertible (2 * MAX + i) and public
revertible (3 * MAX + p), where i is the index in the private kernel's output
and p the index in the tx's note hashes. All use DOM_SEP__NOTE_HASH_NONCE.

- nonce discovery tries every index in all four sections
- the PXE's kernel-less simulation gives revertible note hashes of a tx with
  public calls the private revertible section index
- the partial note test's completion log uses a public revertible nonce index

